25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our grants are quite short-term, and the roads north of the river can be quite unreliable in winter. We must be careful.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The outer wards have lost their bus links, making it very hard for them to reach us. Also, people use the catalogue late at night.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Guess what! People loved the old outreach stops, but the digitisation project from six years ago was a total mess!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant structure is indeed precarious, and last year's vehicle costs were significantly over budget. We should avoid high-maintenance transport.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We have skilled volunteers for repairs, but we lack staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. We cannot simply add more management.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, if the vehicles are so expensive, perhaps a mobile service is too risky for our budget?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, but the people in the outer wards are stranded. They cannot come to us.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Rin,,But the outreach stops were popular! Maybe we just need to do it better this time?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, popularity does not solve the budget overrun. We need a service that doesn't bleed funds by the second year.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, if we move services, we still need people to run them. We have no one to supervise external partners.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, what about the volunteers? Could they help with something like a workshop?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,A workshop stays in one place. It doesn't help the people who have no bus.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Rin,,What about the language groups? They sounded like the ones that lasted six years ago!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, that is an interesting observation. If they are self-sustaining, they fit our financial constraints.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Minako,,Only if they don't require professional supervision from our already stretched staff.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I worry about any plan that relies on the roads or short-term grants.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I still feel the lack of transport is the most urgent gap to fill.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want something that actually works and doesn't get forgotten!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,We need a balance of accessibility and fiscal sustainability.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will support the option that requires the least amount of new supervisory overhead.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
